dles, adding a null check, off-by-one count, changed format string, dropped `s++` — were **all detected**, so the green result isn't vacuous.\n\nTwo things worth flagging:\n\n1. **A harness bug I had to fix, not a translation bug.** My first stdout capture `dup2`'d fd 1 in-process; the cargo test harness kept writing its own progress output to the real fd 1 from another thread, injecting a stray `\\n` into the capture. I moved capture into a forked child so each call gets a private fd 1 and libc buffer. (One other early failure was my own wrong expectation — \"the quick brown fox\" *does* contain an `x`.)\n\n2. **I clobbered `src/lib.rs` mid-session and restored it.** I backed the file up to `/tmp/lib.rs.bak` before mutation testing; `/tmp` is shared, another process overwrote that path with an unrelated file, and my restore copied the foreign file in. I rewrote `src/lib.rs` verbatim from the original content, then confirmed via symbols + full test pass + mutation run that it is the true translation. `mutation_check.sh` now keeps its backup inside the crate. Nothing in `c_src/` was touched (verified).\n\nFinal state: 35 differential tests, 0 failures, 0 compiler warnings."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":768,"cache_read_input_tokens":98103,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":768,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a198aca7-3812-4125-b8b8-0834ae7c3c93","uuid":"8ac3a1af-43be-483f-980d-e0c0e18b98db","timestamp":"2026-08-28T15:04:57.051Z"}
